{"id": 43792790, "slug": "the-dollar", "title": "We Live in a World of Dollars", "subtitle": "September 14th, 2018", "post_date": "2021-11-09T19:30:58.440Z", "audience": "everyone", "wordcount": 528, "reaction_count": 1, "comment_count": 0, "restacks": 1, "reactions": {"\u2764": 1}, "body_html": "<p>Some of us live in a world of dollars.</p><p>As opposed to pounds, or yen, or deutschemarks, we experience the everyday prices for goods and services in units of dollars.</p><p>Everything from our morning coffee, to rent, to our retirement savings is priced in terms of \u201chow many dollar bills is this thing worth?\u201d</p><p>Most of us don\u2019t spend time thinking about the fact that a dollar bill is itself a commodity. It\u2019s just one of those helpful abstractions that comes from thinking that a dollar bill is \u2018money.\u2019</p><p>This abstraction tends to unravel when, like this week, <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-09-12/dalio-says-u-s-in-seventh-inning-as-unfunded-obligations-loom\">famous investors make public predictions</a> that</p><blockquote><p><em>\u201cThe Federal Reserve\u2026will have to print more money to make up for the deficit, have to monetize more and\u2026You easily could have a 30 percent&nbsp;depreciation in the dollar\u201d</em></p></blockquote><p>At Black Snow, while we don\u2019t disagree with Ray\u2019s logic that:</p><p><em>Fed Easing &gt; Lower Interest Rates -&gt; Debt Monetization -&gt; Weaker Dollar</em></p><p>We do disagree with the timeline and path that the dollar may take.</p><p>Given that the Fed is currently tightening (and most other major central banks are easing), the first order pressure on the dollar aught be to strengthen. It\u2019s hard to see the dollar selling off that much in a world where a bank account in New York gets you 2% (and rising) more than a bank account in London, Tokyo or Frankfurt.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png\" width=\"1045\" height=\"559\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://bucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:559,&quot;width&quot;:1045,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Rates and returns.PNG&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Rates and returns.PNG\" title=\"Rates and returns.PNG\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WlBl!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffa2a661c-b197-471b-b5f9-d27d3d13f79e_1045x559.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Further, when you think about what the world would need to look like to get the Fed to switch from tightening:</p><blockquote><p><em>Everything is fine -&gt; Raise Interest Rates -&gt; Shrink the Fed Balance Sheet</em></p></blockquote><p>To easing:</p><blockquote><p><em>Everything is doomed -&gt; Lower Interest Rates -&gt; Buy Assets/Print Money</em></p></blockquote><p>You need a mechanism by which global demand contracts and prompts a change in policy.</p><p>What\u2019s the most likely cause of a contraction in global demand?</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rItd!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f00fc53-d423-4385-a73b-83305e49a919_922x583.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><pictur